00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.350 align:start position:0%
 
so how many of you out there can  remember those arguments you had with  your friends on the playground as a kid  about which console was the best which  games were the best who had the best  exclusive titles trust me i can remember  as a kid arguing sega versus nintendo  and then of course later playstation vs  microsoft versus nintendo and it's funny  how as i've gotten older console wars  and where you play has become so much  less of an issue and i think i know why  you see as a kid so many of us were  limited to just one console my parents  could not understand the need of another  console you have this why do you need  that and so as a result of this we form  teams we form our own little tribe  around our console and we want to fight  for our console to be the best because  after all it's the only one we're gonna  have until the next generation as i've  gotten older though and have had more  disposable income where i can afford  having multiple consoles i'm really  starting to see the absurdity of all of  this and how at the end of the day the  hardware itself actually matters very  little in fact in today's environment  we're seeing a shift away from  exclusives with microsoft going all in  by offering all of their first party  titles on pc day one right alongside the  console counterpart on the other hand  you have nintendo who continues to make  titles exclusively for their platform  alone it wasn't until 2016 that they  finally started making mobile games even  featuring some of their most iconic  characters and somewhere in the middle  you have playstation who have recently  dipped their toe into the pc market by  releasing titles like horizon zero dawn  days gone uncharted legacy of thieves  and even the 2018 god of war it  certainly doesn't seem like their first  party titles will be hitting pc the same  day as consoles in the immediate future  but according to president and ceo jim  ryan it certainly sounds like  playstation is getting ready to make a  massive shift in its gaming business  that will be transformational for the  company and ultimately change the face  of playstation as we know it we have big  plans for fy 22 and beyond with  exponential growth anticipated in the  year just begun and with the opportunity  for our new life services strategy to  boost our pc revenues even more  aggressively in the years to come ryan  recently spoke with investors about the  state of playstation and this talk  included a wide range of subjects  including playstation on pc mobile live  service games the metaverse and even  when he ultimately expects the ps5  supply issues to finally subside which  sadly doesn't look like it will happen  until next year when it comes to  playstation titles on pc there are a few  slides of interest and it actually  starts with the very first slide ryan  shares you can see here they've  identified ps5 and ps4 as their thriving  core business so essentially playstation  currently views home consoles as the  major cog in their thriving core  business next we have a section  highlighting new growth vectors across  three categories commercial portfolio  and audience the one we're focused on in  this video is the third one the audience  which lists pc mobile and beyond console  as growth opportunities we won't talk  much about beyond console in this video  but essentially that's expanding to more  things like movies and tv shows slides  31 through 35 expand on the audience  piece further and there you'll see that  sony is expecting exponential growth  from their pc titles in 2022 and beyond  just take a look at the graph here they  expect the revenue from pc to nearly  quadruple in the 2022 fiscal year alone  now if we jump to slide 34 this one  shows a color-coded graph and judging  from the light blue section we can see  that playstation expects to double the  amount of pc titles they release by  2025. now in the q a that followed  ryan's presentation he was asked for  further clarification on this particular  slide the investor wanted to know if  half the titles would be on pc and  mobile will half of the profits also be  from pc and mobile by 2025. ryan  responded by saying that playstation  studios has historically executed  wonderfully in first party  narrative-rich single-player games but  we have restricted ourselves to a narrow  segment of the gaming market by  expanding to pc and mobile and live  services we have the opportunity to move  from a very narrow segment of the  overall gaming software market to being  present everywhere the opportunity for  significant growth in the number of  people who play our games is potentially  an extremely large one now to me this is  nothing but a good thing 13 year old me  would have been saying you're crazy what  are you thinking they can't put their  games on other consoles they can't put  their games on pc and from where i'm  sitting now i actually think that is not  the truth i agree with ryan here the the  potential for growth and the number of  people who are playing playstation games  is immense and at the end of the day  that's where the money is made trust me  i love hardware i love new console  launches i love the new controllers and  i think they can actually continue to  release new hardware even if they start  releasing their first party games day  and date on pc which doesn't seem like  they're doing that yet but even if they  do go that route i just think there are  enough people out there who prefer the  ecosystem of a console opposed to a pc  that they would continue to choose that  and honestly i would even love a future  where we have like a super low budget  console i actually love what microsoft  did with the xbox series s so i could  see sony releasing that super cheap  super budget friendly console for people  who just want to get into the ecosystem  then you have that sort of middle tier  which is for the wide-ranging gaming  public and then you release titles on pc  as well which is for the people who want  the absolute best top of the line  graphics top of the line performance and  for any of you who know your gaming  history you know that very often  especially early in the life of a  console the console makers very often  have to take a loss on the console and  then hope to make their money back  through things like playstation plus and  the actual sale of the games now  personally i'm in kind of an interesting  boat here where i have had a gaming pc  for a number of years now despite being  a console kid most of my life and i  definitely had a little phase where i  prefer the pc but now i actually find  myself slowly gravitating toward console  again i don't want to get too deep into  it because i know that gets a lot of  arguments going but even as someone  right now who literally has a gaming pc  sitting beside me and a console sitting  beside me there are times even when it's  some of the same games that i will  choose to play a console over the pc now  jim ryan also talked at length about the  upcoming live service games from  playstation saying they currently have  12 in development and he even believes  that if only a portion of these enjoy  what he called a critical and commercial  success the impact over time will be  completely transformational to their  business structure if you've been a fan  of playstation for a while then i  completely get why hearing this could  make you feel a bit uneasy you know  change it's difficult sometimes it  results in good things sometimes it  results in not so good things and i feel  like at least right now i feel like a  lot of playstation's core fan base are  folks who say we do not want these live  service games we want our story driven  last of us infamous uncharted these are  the style of games ghost of tsushima  this is what we want more of so trust me  i get it if you feel a little bit uneasy  and i honestly like i believe ryan and a  lot of folks at playstation i think they  do genuinely care about gamers but at  the end of the day guys it is a company  and we always have to remember  especially for someone in a position  like ryan at the end of the day he  answers to the investors and their  primary goal will always be to make more  money and so with the incredible success  of live service titles playstation would  be foolish not to try but again to so  many of us our love of playstation comes  from those single-player story driven  titles and i'll be completely straight  with you no one knows for sure what  playstation would do if these live  service games take off do they decide to  say hey you know what let's put even  more resources into this and let's kind  of slowly phase out of doing these first  party single player games that's not  what they're saying right now and  personally i don't see them abandoning  those core first party story driven  games anytime soon for one i think you  look at some of the acquisitions they've  been making they continue to build up  their stable of first party developers  by acquiring more talent like insomniac  house mark and blue point developers who  excel at those single player story  driven games how smart not so much in  the story department but in gameplay  top-notch gameplay and then hey with  returnal they did start to try and do a  little bit more with the story as well  of course bluepoint we know about their  history importing various titles they're  an incredibly talented studio that can  help in a lot of different areas plus  playstation is also in the process of  acquiring bungie whom they have said  they expect to be instrumental in  helping with these live service  endeavors so my point here is at least  right now it's not like they're taking  the team from sucker punch who made  ghosts of tsushima and saying hey we're  going to put you guys on a live service  game now or they're taking the team who  made the last of us and saying all right  you're doing live service now from  everything we've seen and heard so far  they are interested in growing the  overall business and so as they grow the  overall business a lot of times the only  way to do that is by doing new things  trying some new things while keeping  that core business focus firmly in their  view honestly the entire presentation  and subsequent q a with the investors i  think is worth a watch if you're a fan  of playstation or even just a fan of  gaming in general and kind of  understanding more about the business  side and what they're talking about i  say behind the scenes but i guess it's  not really behind the scenes because  this one's public but it definitely puts  you more in that business mindset and me  at 12 years old would have never  imagined me making a video like this  saying some of these things but i truly  believe console wars they're becoming a  thing of the past brands and services  they provide they are becoming the focus  they are becoming far more important  than the hardware itself it's about the  games it's about the ip it's about the  service much more so than the hardware i  can't wait to hear what you guys think  about this let me know in the comments  below are you looking forward to more pc  games from playstation or do you wish  they would stick to just making their  games for console as always thank you  all so much for watching i'll talk to  you again soon

